{"builder":"Build the new tool `jsonl-lint` as an npm workspace for issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 and open one pull request. Right now `packages/` does not exist, and the root README says \"No tools yet\".\n\n1. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json` with: `\"name\": \"jsonl-lint\"`, `\"type\": \"module\"`, `\"private\": true`, `\"bin\": { \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }`, `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22\" }` and `\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }`. Do not add `dependencies`. Do not add `devDependencies` either.\n2. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js`, a plain ES module that exports `lint(text)`. Split `text` on `\\n` and strip a trailing `\\r` from each row. Rows numbered from 1. Skip any row that is empty or only whitespace, but still count it in the line numbers. Run `JSON.parse` on every other row. Each row that throws adds `{ line, error }` to the result, where `error` is the parse error message (a non-empty string). Return the array in line order, or `[]` if every row is valid. A last row with no trailing newline is still checked, so a torn row such as `{\"a\":` gets reported. A trailing newline at the end of the file must not produce a phantom row.\n3. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` and start it with `#!/usr/bin/env node`. It reads `process.argv[2]`.\n   - If there is no argument, write a usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n   - If the file cannot be read (missing, for example), write a message naming the file to stderr and exit 2.\n   - Otherwise call `lint`. For each error, print `<file>:<line>: <error>` to stdout, one per line, with `<file>` exactly as given on the command line. Exit 1 if there were any errors, 0 if none.\n   Make the file executable (`chmod +x`, and check that git records mode 100755).\n4. Add `node:test` tests in `packages/jsonl-lint/test/` (e.g. `test/lint.test.js`, `test/cli.test.js`) using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`. Cover:\n   - a clean file → `[]` and exit 0\n   - a bad middle row → reported at the right 1-based line, exit 1, output line `<file>:<line>: ...`\n   - a torn last row with no trailing newline → reported\n   - blank lines → skipped, but line numbers still count them\n   - exit codes 0, 1 and 2: no argument, and a missing file with a non-empty stderr\n   For the CLI tests, run the bin with `child_process.spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, file])`, using fixture files written to `os.tmpdir()`.\n5. Write `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md`: what the tool does, how to use it, the output format, the exit codes (0/1/2) and the `lint(text)` API. Edit the root `README.md`: under \"What is here\", replace the \"No tools yet\" bullet with a bullet listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and a one-line description.\n6. From the repo root, run `npm install` so that `package-lock.json` includes the new workspace (CI runs `npm ci`, which fails on a stale lock). Then run `npm ci && npm test` and confirm both pass. Also run the bin by hand on a clean file, a bad file, a missing file and no argument.\n7. Commit everything: the package files, the tests, both READMEs and `package-lock.json`. Push, then open one PR against suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow on the PR head to finish. If it fails, fix the cause, push again and wait until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the PR head of the single PR for https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 and run `npm ci` at the repo root. Write fixtures to a temp directory. There is one check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\"\nCreate these fixtures:\n- clean.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n`\n- bad.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{bad\\n{\"c\":3}\\nnope\\n`: errors expected on lines 3 and 5. Line 2 is blank.\n- torn.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":` with no trailing newline: error expected on line 2.\n- blank.jsonl = `\\n{\"a\":1}\\n   \\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n`\nFor each fixture, run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <path>` and record stdout and the exit code.\nPASS when all of these hold:\n- clean.jsonl and blank.jsonl exit 0 and print no `<path>:<n>:` lines.\n- bad.jsonl exits 1 and prints exactly two error lines: one starting `<path>:3: ` and one starting `<path>:5: `, each followed by non-empty error text.\n- torn.jsonl exits 1 and prints one line starting `<path>:2: ` with non-empty error text.\nFAIL on any other exit code, a missing or extra error line, or wrong line numbers (including blank lines being reported, or line numbers that don't count blank lines).\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\"\nRun `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl`, then run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` with no argument. Capture stderr and the exit code for each.\nPASS if both exit 2 with non-empty stderr. FAIL otherwise.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\"\nRun `node --input-type=module -e \"import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n'), lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\nbad\\n')]))\"`.\nPASS if `lint` is an exported function and the output is: first an empty array, then an array with one object whose `line` is 2 and that has an `error` field. FAIL if the import fails, `lint` is not exported, or the shape differs.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\"\nRead `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json` with node.\nPASS when all of these hold:\n- `name` === \"jsonl-lint\"\n- `type` === \"module\"\n- `scripts.test` is `node --test` (optionally followed by test paths)\n- `dependencies` is absent or empty\n- `npm test -w jsonl-lint` passes\n- the test files import `node:test`, and among them have tests covering a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes (inspect the test names and bodies while they run)\nFAIL if any of these is missing.\n\nCheck 5 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\"\nRun `test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` and `grep -n jsonl-lint README.md`.\nPASS if the file exists and the root README mentions jsonl-lint. FAIL otherwise.\n\nCheck 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\"\nRun `gh pr list -R suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --state open --search \"102 in:body\"` and `gh pr view <n> --json body,headRefOid,statusCheckRollup`. At the head, run `npm ci && npm test`.\nPASS when all of these hold:\n- exactly one PR is for this issue\n- its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`\n- local `npm test` exits 0\n- the `test` workflow check for headRefOid has conclusion SUCCESS\nFAIL if there is more than one PR or none, the body text is missing, npm test fails, or the workflow is failing, pending or absent for that head SHA.\n\nAdvisory\n- Check that `bin/jsonl-lint.js` has a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang and git mode 100755.\n- Check that `package-lock.json` includes the workspace.\n- Check that CRLF rows are not reported as errors."}